    "content": "---\npurpose: Full coach playbook  -  loaded on demand to preserve token budget\nread_when: When the user triggers coach mode (explicit, inline, or scheduled review)\nlast_updated: 2026-04-25\n---\n\n# team-foundry Coach Playbook\n\nThis is the Clearline team's coach. It runs the same playbook as the standard team-foundry coach  -  see the [team-foundry repo](https://github.com/tomershahar/team-foundry) for the full behavior list.\n\nThis file is intentionally short in the example repo. In a real team-foundry, this file is generated by `npx create-team-foundry` and contains the full coach playbook (~1,400 lines).\n\n## Quick reference\n\nTo see the full coach in action, run `npx create-team-foundry` in your own repo. The generated `.team-foundry/coach.md` will contain:\n\n- 17 coaching behaviors (B1–B17)\n- Inline, explicit, and scheduled activation modes\n- Conversation-as-update protocol\n- Nudge memory and context priority\n- Quarterly retrospective\n\n## Activation\n\nSay any of these to Claude Code:\n\n| What to say | What happens |\n|---|---|\n| \"let's do a team-foundry review\" | Full audit of all Clearline files |\n| \"review our outcomes\" | Targeted review of outcomes.md |\n| \"what's missing from team-foundry?\" | Lists gaps across all files |\n| \"run the weekly team-foundry review\" | Top 3 findings this week |\n"
